          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 66,
              "v_start": 1,
              "v_end": 1,
              "text": "All lands — Ye people of all nations. He invites the Gentile world, to the contemplation and celebration of God's works."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 66,
              "v_start": 6,
              "v_end": 6,
              "text": "We — Our nation, or our ancestors, in whose loins we then were."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 66,
              "v_start": 10,
              "v_end": 10,
              "text": "Proved us — As it were in a burning furnace; and with a design to purge out our dross."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 66,
              "v_start": 11,
              "v_end": 11,
              "text": "Net — Which our enemies laid for us."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 66,
              "v_start": 12,
              "v_end": 12,
              "text": "To ride — To use us like slaves."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "second",
          "ref": "2 Timothy 2:8-15",
          "refKey": "2Tim.2.8-2Tim.2.15",
          "tags": {
            "theme": [
              "faithfulness",
              "resurrection-and-life",
              "suffering-and-endurance",
              "word-of-god"
            ],
            "image": [
              "prison-and-chains"
            ],
            "mood": [
              "assurance",
              "exhortation"
            ]
          },
          "notes": [
            {
              "chapter": 2,
              "v_start": 8,
              "v_end": 8,
              "text": "Of the seed of David — This one genealogy attend to."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 2,
              "v_start": 9,
              "v_end": 9,
              "text": "Is not bound — Not hindered in its course."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 2,
              "v_start": 10,
              "v_end": 10,
              "text": "Therefore — Encouraged by this, that \"the word of God be not bound.\" I endure all things - See the spirit of a real Christian? Who would not wish to be likeminded? Salvation is deliverance from all evil; glory, the enjoyment of all good."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 2,
              "v_start": 11,
              "v_end": 11,
              "text": "Dead with him — Dead to sin, and ready to die for him."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 2,
              "v_start": 12,
              "v_end": 12,
              "text": "If we deny him — To escape suffering for him."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 2,
              "v_start": 13,
              "v_end": 13,
              "text": "If we believe not — That is, though some believe not, God will make good all his promises to them that do believe. He cannot deny himself - His word cannot fail."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 2,
              "v_start": 14,
              "v_end": 14,
              "text": "Remind them — Who are under thy charge. O how many unnecessary things are thus unprofitably, nay hurtfully, contended for."
            },
            {
              "chapter": 2,
              "v_start": 15,
              "v_end": 15,
              "text": "A workman that needeth not to be ashamed — Either of unfaithfulness or unskilfulness. Rightly dividing the word of truth - Duly explaining and applying the whole scripture, so as to give each hearer his due portion. But they that give one part of the gospel to all (the promises and comforts to unawakened, hardened, scoffing men) have real need to be ashamed."
            }
          ]
        },
